{"toolCallId":"call_b8a439698e2942009d3c3d89153befb5","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"111: * schema and no spec-doc anchors, so they are exempt from the _memory-block and\n112: * anchor-sufficiency gates. The numbered levels list research/research.md as a\n140:// anchors are required whenever the document is present. decision-record.md is\n446:    const anchors = [];\n455:        // Matching inside code would read those examples as real anchors and report the\n490:            anchors.push({\n507:    return { anchors, errors };\n782:    const matches = parsed.anchors.filter((anchor) => anchor.id === mergePlan.targetAnchor);\n847: * log anchor, anchors and comments included, so the count matches what an\n886:    const binding = parseAnchors(content).anchors.find((anchor) => anchor.id === 'binding');\n963:        // continue checking whatever anchors were partially parsed, letting\n964:        // documents with corrupt anchor structure pass sufficiency validation.\n974:        const anchorMap = new Map(parsed.anchors.map((anchor) => [anchor.id, anchor]));\n987:        for (const anchor of parsed.anchors) {\n1015:            // uncited. Fall back to the document body when no anchors are present.\n1016:            const citedResearch = parsed.anchors.length > 0\n1017:                ? parsed.anchors.some((anchor) => looksLikeCitation(anchor.body))\n1031:            for (const anchor of parsed.anchors.filter((entry) => entry.id.startsWith('adr-'))) {\n1042:    return createResult('SPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY', diagnostics, 'All targeted spec-doc anchors meet the sufficiency baseline');\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"02d7e8","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
